From: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>
Date: Thu Sep 10 15:18:01 2026 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Fix mmap_read_lock for protected-VM THP adjustment

In pkvm_mem_abort(), __pkvm_pin_user_pages() takes and then drops the
mmap_read_lock() right before __pkvm_pages_to_ppages() is called,
leaving the stage-1 page table parsing in transparent_hugepage_adjust()
unprotected.

If the guest shares the unpinned memory back, the host allocator will
blindly use those pages for host private data while the guest retains
access, compromising host isolation.

Hoist mmap_read_lock() into pkvm_mem_abort() to span both page pinning
and THP adjustments continuously.

Bug: 559603594
Fixes: 5d9808b9071c ("ANDROID: KVM: arm64: THP support for pKVM guests")
Change-Id: Ib06098b1e2edf013406042cdcd0d77d5b77f2522
Signed-off-by: Vincent Donnefort <vdonnefort@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note - 2026-11-02, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin. The fix holds the mmap read lock from
pin_user_pages() through the THP adjustment instead of dropping it
immediately. The pin's pkvm_mem_abort() mid-section is an older
vintage (maple-tree reservation + retry loop, no mmu_lock read
section, no kvm_pinned_pages_iter_first, no negative page_size
retry), so the exit-path graph differs from upstream: the
-EHWPOISON/-EFAULT/-EIO branch unlocks apply as-is; the third
unlock is re-placed right after transparent_hugepage_adjust() and
before the maple-tree reservation/retry section (upstream releases
after its mmu_lock read-section) - identical hold window
(GUP -> THP adjust), released before account_locked_vm(), which
takes the mmap write lock internally (a held read lock there would
self-deadlock). Every remaining exit (unpin / free_ppage /
err_unlock / retry) sits after the release point. Upstream hunks
4-5 (__pkvm_pin_user_pages / __pkvm_pgtable_stage2_split) are
skipped: both functions are absent at the pin (as triaged).
Verified: strict git apply on the pin replica + exit-path walk.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 4863da38964d78a50d5fffa4dfebdc985e581e83
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class B, RESHAPED for the pin; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
index a152d646d..fc4fe8a47 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/mmu.c
@@ -1731,14 +1731,15 @@ static int pkvm_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t *fault_ipa,
 
 	mmap_read_lock(mm);
 	ret = pin_user_pages(hva, 1, flags, &page);
-	mmap_read_unlock(mm);
 
 	if (ret == -EHWPOISON) {
 		kvm_send_hwpoison_signal(hva, PAGE_SHIFT);
 		ret = 0;
+		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
 		goto free_ppage;
 	} else if (ret != 1) {
 		ret = -EFAULT;
+		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
 		goto free_ppage;
 	} else if (kvm->arch.pkvm.enabled && !PageSwapBacked(page)) {
 		/*
@@ -1756,6 +1757,7 @@ static int pkvm_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t *fault_ipa,
 		 * prevent try_to_unmap() from succeeding.
 		 */
 		ret = -EIO;
+		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
 		goto unpin;
 	}
 
@@ -1766,6 +1768,7 @@ static int pkvm_mem_abort(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, phys_addr_t *fault_ipa,
 						fault_ipa);
 	page = pfn_to_page(pfn);
 
+		mmap_read_unlock(mm);
 retry:
 	if (size)
 		*size = page_size;
